### Mobile app sign-up / login against the Identity service.
### In Development the code is also returned as "devOtp" (and always written to the log when email isn't set up).

@id = http://localhost:5001
@email = test.user@example.com
@password = Passw0rd!x
@scope = openid profile auctionApp IdentityServerApi offline_access

### 1. Sign up (username is made from the first name: "Test User" -> "test", "test2", ...)
POST {{id}}/api/account/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Test User",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "phoneNumber": "+919876543210",
  "password": "{{password}}",
  "acceptTerms": true
}

### 2. Log in with email + password.
###    Trusted device (device_token from step 3) -> tokens. Otherwise -> 400 with code OTP_REQUIRED + challengeId.
POST {{id}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=bmw_password&client_id=mobileApp&scope={{scope}}&username={{email}}&password={{password}}&device_id=my-phone

### 3. Enter the emailed code. remember_device=true also returns "deviceToken" (skip the code for 30 days).
POST {{id}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=bmw_otp&client_id=mobileApp&scope={{scope}}&challenge_id=PASTE_CHALLENGE_ID&otp=123456&device_id=my-phone&remember_device=true

### Resend the login code (30 s cooldown)
POST {{id}}/api/account/otp/resend
Content-Type: application/json

{ "challengeId": "PASTE_CHALLENGE_ID" }

### The signed-in user
GET {{id}}/api/account/me
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN

### Refresh ("Remember me"). Refresh tokens are one-time: use the new one each time.
POST {{id}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&client_id=mobileApp&refresh_token=PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN

### Log out (revoke the refresh token)
POST {{id}}/connect/revocation
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

client_id=mobileApp&token=PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN&token_type_hint=refresh_token

### Forgot password -> emails a code
POST {{id}}/api/account/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}" }

### Reset password (signs out all devices)
POST {{id}}/api/account/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "otp": "123456", "newPassword": "NewPassw0rd!" }

### Google / Apple: id_token from the phone. Apple also needs the raw nonce.
POST {{id}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=bmw_external&client_id=mobileApp&scope={{scope}}&provider=google&id_token=PASTE_GOOGLE_ID_TOKEN

### The token works everywhere: gateway -> auction service echoes the username
POST http://localhost:6001/auctions/test
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN

### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### ADMIN – seller accounts (role admin only; Swagger: {{id}}/swagger)
### The admin is seeded from user-secrets (Seed:AdminEmail / Seed:AdminPassword, see RUN_LOCAL.md 5A).
### 1) Sign in as the admin with steps 2 + 3 above (email + password, then the code) → copy access_token here.
### ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
@adminToken = PASTE_ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN

### ── Seller applications ("Want to sell?" form in the app) ──
### The app sends this (signed out, or signed in with the buyer's token → linked to the account). Admins get an email.
POST {{id}}/api/seller-applications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ravi Kumar",
  "email": "ravi.seller@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+919812345678",
  "countryCode": "IN",
  "city": "Hyderabad",
  "businessType": "Shop",
  "sells": "Parts",
  "businessName": "Ravi Auto Parts",
  "businessAddress": "12 MG Road, Ameerpet",
  "taxId": "36ABCDE1234F1Z5",
  "message": "Used bumpers and headlamps"
}

### New requests (status: New, InReview, Approved, Rejected; search: name, email, business name or city)
GET {{id}}/api/admin/seller-applications?status=New
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### One request
GET {{id}}/api/admin/seller-applications/PASTE_APPLICATION_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Review it: InReview, or Rejected with a note (the applicant sees a rejection note in Profile).
### To approve, create the seller below (POST /api/admin/sellers with the same email) or make-seller for a signed-in
### buyer (userId in the request): that marks the request Approved automatically.
PATCH {{id}}/api/admin/seller-applications/PASTE_APPLICATION_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "Rejected", "adminNote": "Please add your GST number and apply again." }

### Create a seller → 201 { seller, message, devInviteCode (Development only) }. The seller gets an email with a
### one-time code (72 h) and sets the password in the app: Login → "Got a seller invite? Set your password".
POST {{id}}/api/admin/sellers
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Ravi Kumar",
  "email": "ravi.seller@example.com",
  "phoneNumber": "+919812345678",
  "countryCode": "IN",
  "businessName": "Ravi Auto Parts",
  "city": "Hyderabad"
}

### List / search sellers (name, email, username or business name)
GET {{id}}/api/admin/sellers?search=ravi&page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### All accounts with their role – find a buyer's id for make-seller
GET {{id}}/api/admin/users?search=ravi
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Send the invite code again (before the seller has set a password; 30 s cooldown)
POST {{id}}/api/admin/sellers/PASTE_SELLER_ID/invite
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Update or disable a seller (disabled: true signs them out everywhere; false enables again)
PATCH {{id}}/api/admin/sellers/PASTE_SELLER_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "disabled": true, "city": "Secunderabad" }

### Upgrade an existing buyer to seller (the app picks it up at the next token refresh / when reopened)
POST {{id}}/api/admin/users/PASTE_USER_ID/make-seller
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### New seller sets their password with the invite code (same endpoint as reset password)
POST {{id}}/api/account/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ravi.seller@example.com", "otp": "PASTE_INVITE_CODE", "newPassword": "Sell3r!Passw0rd" }

### A buyer's (or seller's) token on an admin endpoint → 403 { "message": "Only admins can do this.", "code": "ADMIN_ONLY" }
GET {{id}}/api/admin/sellers
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_BUYER_ACCESS_TOKEN
